"Summarizes a decision problem through controllable choices, uncertain quantities, value objectives and informational dependencies.\n\nUse when: Frame uncertainty before building a large decision tree. Clarify what a decision maker knows and which variables affect value.\n\nAvoid when: Detailed path-by-path narration is essential to the audience.\n\nVisual grammar: Decision, chance and value nodes use distinct shapes. Arcs into decisions show information available when choosing. Arcs into chance or value nodes show probabilistic or functional dependence.\n\nBuild: List the decision variables, uncertainties and valued consequences. Order decisions and identify information available before each one. Connect only relevant dependencies and document the associated models.\n\nCheck: The dependency structure is acyclic for a standard influence diagram. Information arcs reflect actual observation timing. Value nodes include all material objectives and consequence dependencies.\n\nPitfalls: Reading every arc as physical causation. Adding a feedback loop that violates the evaluation semantics.\n\nExample: A stock decision uses a demand forecast, uncertain demand and purchase costs to determine profit, with forecast availability explicitly shown.\n\nAlternatives: Decision tree, Decision requirements diagram."
